hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17645","Yahya ibn Adam and Ibn Abi Bukayr said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubshi ibn Junadah, Yahya ibn Adam said: al-Saluli, and he had witnessed the Farewell Hajj, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Ali is from me and I am from him, and none discharges on my behalf except me or 'Ali. And Ibn Abi Bukayr said: None settles my debt on my behalf except me or 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"17646","al-Zubayri narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us the like of it."
"17647","And he narrated it to us, meaning al-Zubayri: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubshi ibn Junadah the like of it. He said: I said to Abu Ishaq: I heard it from him. He said: He stood over us on a horse of his in our gathering in the cemetery of al-Sabi'."
"17648","Yahya ibn Adam and Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubshi ibn Junadah, Yahya said: and he was among those who witnessed the Farewell Hajj, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said on the third: And those who shorten."
"17649","Yahya ibn Adam and Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubshi ibn Junadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks without poverty, it is as though he eats embers."
"17650","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubshi ibn Junadah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever asks without poverty, and he mentioned the like of it."
"17651","Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us: Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubshi ibn Junadah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Ali is from me and I am from him, and none discharges on my behalf except me or 'Ali."
"17652","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubshi ibn Junadah al-Saluli, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Ali is from me and I am from him, and none discharges on my behalf except me or 'Ali. Sharik said: I said to Abu Ishaq: Where did you hear it from him? He said: In such-and-such place, I do not remember it."
"17653","Abu Ahmad narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubshi ibn Junadah al-Saluli, and he had witnessed the Farewell Hajj, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Ali is from me and I am from him, and none discharges on my behalf except me or 'Ali."
